## 1. Root causes

**Greeting still on the left in Arabic.** Not a `textAlign` problem. The title stack in `DashboardHeader` is a **column**, so its `alignItems` resolves on the *horizontal* cross axis — and under `direction: 'rtl'` Yoga flips that axis, so `flex-end` means **left**. The code set `direction: 'rtl'` **and** `alignItems: 'flex-end'`: a double mirror that pinned the whole block (greeting + name) to the left edge in Arabic, whatever each `Text` said.

**Arabic tab order wrong (Profile far right).** The previous fix reversed the `<Screen>` array when the app locale and `I18nManager.isRTL` disagreed. That can never work: this navigator is wrapped in Expo Router's `withLayoutContext`, whose route list comes from the router's own file-system order (`useSortedScreens` → `getSortedChildren`) — our children are re-sorted by name, so the reversal was a **no-op**. The bar stayed LTR and Profile sat at the far right. The test passed because it only checked "we reversed the array".

**`Published 3`.** The KPI card was `drOverview.published` (a *status*) while the neighbouring card used `nav.myCourses` (a *tab label*) for the total. Nothing described "how many courses".

**Default contact always selectable.** The switch never copied anything — it tells delivery to read `profiles.contact_whatsapp/telegram/phone`. With all three empty the course inherited nothing, so the Subscribe sheet showed no doctor contact at all. The UI never consulted the profile.

**Slow resume.** The pipeline was already coalesced/bounded, but every resume still fetched things that provably cannot change while the app sits in the background: the TLS pin probe (up to 5 s) and, once its 10-minute window lapsed, the platform attestation round-trip. There was no notion of *what a check measures*, only "run everything".

**PDF delivery failure.** Not proven. There is no PHP runtime in this environment and no access to the live server, so I did not invent a cause. What I found: every refusal was collapsed to the generic message, `ApiException`'s machine-readable code was **discarded by `ErrorHandler`** (so even `watermark_busy` arrived as `api_error`), the audit row only ever said stage `mint`, the real exception class/message was never recorded, and the render had no time budget — after the layer-token bump invalidated every cached copy, a 30 s `max_execution_time` on shared hosting would produce a **PHP fatal with no JSON at all**, which is exactly this symptom.

## 2–3. What changed, and verification

**Greeting** — stack is pinned to `direction: 'ltr'` with `alignItems: isRTL ? 'flex-end' : 'flex-start'` (one physical mirror); text still follows the locale; account name untouched (never translated). Greeting line now uses a dedicated `home.hello` ("Hello" / "مرحباً") so it no longer doubles as a role label.

**Tabs** — iOS uses the library's own `layoutDirection={appRTL ? 'rtl' : 'ltr'}`, applied natively as SwiftUI `.environment(\.layoutDirection)`; the array reversal and the `I18nManager` second-guess are gone. The JS bar (Android/web) keeps its single `direction: 'ltr'` + `row-reverse` mirror. Route names, icons, active state, deep links, `initialRouteName` and `backBehavior` unchanged.

**Instructor KPI** — the count card is `drOverview.courses` (`عدد الدورات`) with `totalCourses`; the published figure keeps its **unchanged** scope but is labelled `drOverview.publishedCourses` (`دورات منشورة`) so it cannot be read as the total.

**Default contact** — three states (`unknown` while loading / `available` / `missing`); disabled, dimmed, `accessibilityState` + `accessibilityHint`; hints in both locales; "usable" means real digits/handle, so a blank or garbage value does not count; a *confirmed* missing state switches the form to custom contact (never while loading, never touching entered values).

**Resume** — `runSecurityChecks({ scope })`: `full` for session start, manual, **pre-video** and post-update; `resume` for background→foreground and the periodic tick. Every detector that a backgrounded app can invalidate (VPN, proxy, debugger, developer options, screen recording, overlay, root, tamper, hooking frameworks) still runs every time. Only server-attested, already-TTL'd evidence is reused (Play Integrity/App Attest 10 min; a **verified** TLS pin for 90 s — an inconclusive probe is never recorded; policy rows 5 min). Per-detector timings are returned and printed as `[SecurityCheck][timing] scope=… total=…ms sslReused=…`. Full table in [SECURITY_VERIFICATION_LIFECYCLE.md](docs/SECURITY_VERIFICATION_LIFECYCLE.md).

**PDF** — stage codes on every refusal (`engine_unavailable`, `pdf_parse`, `render_failed`, `output_missing`, `publish_failed`, `schema`, `source_*`, `watermark_busy`), the real cause recorded as `cause` in the `material_pdf_failed` audit row, `ErrorHandler` now surfaces a coded `ApiException` instead of `api_error`, a bounded render budget (`PDF_WATERMARK_TIME_LIMIT_SECONDS`, default 90, restored afterwards), the registry INSERT wrapped so a missing column can't masquerade as a generic 500, and an end-to-end CLI probe [diagnose-pdf-delivery.php](backend/scripts/diagnose-pdf-delivery.php). Fail-closed is untouched: no unwatermarked fallback anywhere.

**Tests:** `npx tsc --noEmit` clean · `npm run test:state` 79 passed · `node scripts/run-all-tests.cjs` **116 passed, 1 failed** · `npx eslint` 0 errors (38 pre-existing warnings) · `node backend/scripts/validate-php-syntax.js` 302/303 (only `vendor/tecnickcom/.../tcpdf_static.php`, pre-existing and git-ignored).

The one failure is **pre-existing**: `dependencyLicensePolicy.test.cjs` — the committed `DEPENDENCY_LICENSE_AUDIT.md` doesn't name TCPDF/LGPL (an earlier session replaced it). I didn't fabricate replacement content.

## 4–8. Honesty about what I could not verify

- **No physical device.** I cannot confirm the greeting edge, the native tab order or resume behaviour on an iPhone from here. The tab mirror in particular should be checked on device: `layoutDirection` affects the SwiftUI tab bar, not RN content layout.
- **Resume timings: not measured.** I have no device and no before/after numbers, so I won't state any. The structural change is measurable via the new `[SecurityCheck][timing]` line (set `EXPO_PUBLIC_SECURITY_DIAGNOSTICS=1`), which reports `scope`, `total`, `sslReused` and the three slowest detectors.
- **PDF stage: still unidentified.** The exact failing stage will be named by `php backend/scripts/diagnose-pdf-delivery.php <material_id>` (or by the `stage` field of the newest `material_pdf_failed` audit row). Until that runs on the live server, the regression is **not** confirmed fixed — I added the diagnosis and the most likely fix (render budget) rather than claiming success.

## 9–12. Backend, deployment, rollback

**Backend files modified:** [MaterialDeliveryController.php](backend/src/Controllers/MaterialDeliveryController.php), [ErrorHandler.php](backend/src/Middleware/ErrorHandler.php), [PdfWatermarkService.php](backend/src/Services/PdfWatermarkService.php), [PDF_WATERMARK_DEPLOYMENT.md](backend/docs/PDF_WATERMARK_DEPLOYMENT.md). **New:** [diagnose-pdf-delivery.php](backend/scripts/diagnose-pdf-delivery.php).

**Upload to the live server:** exactly those three PHP files plus the script (upload the script outside the document root as with the other CLI scripts). No route, schema or controller-contract change.

**Migration / config:** no new migration; the `035` fallbacks are untouched. Optional env `PDF_WATERMARK_TIME_LIMIT_SECONDS=90`. Required PHP extensions are unchanged (zlib, mbstring; FPDI/TCPDF already vendored) — `watermark-diagnostics.php` reports them.

**Rollback:** restore the three PHP files from `git` (the changes are additive: codes, logging, a try/catch and a time-limit wrapper — the render logic itself is untouched). Client-side rollback is a normal rebuild of the previous commit.

**Other files changed:** [DashboardHeader.tsx](src/components/DashboardHeader.tsx), [RoleTabShell.ios.tsx](src/components/navigation/RoleTabShell.ios.tsx), [dr-overview.tsx](src/app/(app)/(doctor)/dr-overview.tsx), [dashboard.tsx](src/app/(app)/(student)/dashboard.tsx), [course-builder/[id].tsx](src/app/(app)/course-builder/[id].tsx), [lesson/[id].tsx](src/app/(app)/lesson/[id].tsx), [resources.ts](src/lib/i18n/resources.ts), [security.ts](src/lib/security.ts), [SecurityContext.tsx](src/lib/SecurityContext.tsx), [store.ts](src/lib/store.ts), the lifecycle doc, and 9 existing + 2 new test suites.

