Investigation complete, with one optimisation implemented and verified. Here is the report.

## A. Root causes (ranked, confirmed first)

**1. The security verdict gate serialises all protected traffic at launch and on resume — the biggest structural cause.** `SecurityContext` runs one evaluation; `src/client/php.ts` (`apiFetchOnce`) defers every protected request behind `isSecurityLocked()` for up to `NETWORK_LOCK_DEFER_MAX_MS = 20_000`. So the launch order is *session → security verdict → profile → dashboard batch* — three serial network phases, and phase 2 is bounded by the slowest detector (Play Integrity and the TLS probe can each take up to `DETECTOR_TIMEOUT_MS = 10 s`). Confirmed in code, not measured on a device. Two mitigations from the previous round are present and verified: the security config GET is single-flight and **started before** the detector batch, and `setIsLoading(false)` runs **before** `checkRevocation()`, so the device-binding call no longer blocks first paint.

**2. The student's enrollment list was re-downloaded by six screens (confirmed, fixed now).** `getMySubscriptions()` embeds the full course row plus doctor and category, and was called by Dashboard, Explore, My Courses, Profile, Course details and the Lesson player. A normal journey downloaded that same fat list 4–6 times in a few seconds, each with its own loading state.

**3. Screens blanked to a spinner on every focus (already fixed, re-verified):** 8 in-scope screens now use `useStaleWhileRevalidateFocus`; zero blanking focus loaders remain in the covered set.

**4. Video Library fetched once per keystroke (already fixed, re-verified):** debounce + typed/queries state split; input bound to what is typed.

**Suspected, not confirmed (documented, not implemented):** the `courses(*)` embed inside `getMySubscriptions` makes the list payload far larger than the cards need; catalogue + categories still load with the dashboard's first paint; `courses` has no `(status, created_at)` index for the published catalogue (needs a production migration, so out of bounds without your approval).

## B. Can it be made faster? Yes — with a clear split

*Already achieved (verified):* the security config duplicate, focus blanking and per-keystroke fetching are gone; the enrollment list now costs **one** download per burst instead of six.
*Realistic next gains:* narrowing the `courses(*)` embed (payload/parse, needs consumer-by-consumer verification and payload measurement), deferring catalogue/categories until after first paint, and the `courses(status, created_at)` index. None of these can be honestly sized without real-device or server numbers.
*Hard limit:* the security gate. Shortening it means weakening fail-closed verification, which I did not do.

## C. Before / after evidence

| Measurement | Before | After | How |
|---|---|---|---|
| Enrollment downloads, 6-screen burst (Dashboard→My Courses→Course→Lesson→Profile→Explore) | 6 | **1** | executed module, stubbed transport, counted calls |
| Enrollment downloads, 3 surfaces mounting together | 3 | **1** | same |
| Re-read inside 30 s / after 30 s | 1 / 1 | **0 / 1** | same |
| Downloads after enroll / sign-out / account switch | — | 1 (invalidated) | same |
| `get-security-policies` GETs per evaluation | 2 | **1** | single call site + single-flight assertions |
| In-scope screens blanking on focus | 8 | **0** | source assertions |
| GETs typing a 7-char query | 7 | **1** | debounce assertions |
| Cold-launch stage durations (js-start / session / verdict / profile / screen-data) | — | ⚠️ **not measured** | new dev-only timeline prints them on your device |
| Endpoint latency, payload bytes, SQL time, FPS | — | ⚠️ **not measured** | no server access; no physical device |

## D. Screen-by-screen

| Screen | Confirmed bottleneck | Change |
|---|---|---|
| Student Dashboard | enrollment list re-downloaded per visit | reads through the 30 s cache → 1 per burst |
| Explore | same | same |
| My Courses | same | same |
| Student Profile | same | same |
| Course details | none found (3 reads, enrollment extras already started concurrently with the course read) | enrollment read now cached; ordering preserved |
| Lesson player | same enrollment re-download | cached |
| Video Library | none remaining | no change |
| Students, Doctor Courses, Doctor Overview, Notifications | none found (parallel reads + SWR) | no change |
| Offline Library / Offline Course | no API on focus (local store) | no change |

## E. Remaining priorities

1. **Measure on-device with the new timeline** (zero effort, highest decision value): tells you whether the verdict, the profile call or screen data dominates. Confidence high.
2. **Defer catalogue/categories to after first paint** (low effort, low risk, moderate impact on perceived cold start).
3. **Narrow the `courses(*)` embed** (medium effort, medium risk because 6 consumers read different fields, high impact on payload/parse). Do it with payload measurements.
4. **`courses(status, created_at)` index** (tiny effort, tiny risk, impact only on a large catalogue; needs a migration + your approval).

## F. Files and deployment

**Backend: none.** This round changed **zero PHP files**, so there is **nothing new to upload**, and **no database migration** is required. (The tree still carries the earlier, uncommitted PDF-upload/cleanup backend work — `backend/src/Controllers/CourseController.php`, `LessonMaterialController.php`, `UploadIntegrityService.php`, `MaterialFileCleanupService.php`, `StorageService.php`, `DataController.php`, `RpcController.php`, `StorageController.php`, `PdfWatermarkService.php`, `backend/routes/api.php`, `backend/scripts/*` — that is from the previous request and still needs deploying if it has not been.)

