**Config/dependencies:** none — no new packages, no env vars.

A **frontend rebuild** is required (JS bundle only; no `ios/` changes, no `pod install`).

## G. Verdict

* **Biggest confirmed cause of loading delays:** the security gate that holds every protected request at launch/resume, followed by the repeated enrollment download (now fixed).
* **Most effective safe improvement made:** one 30 s, account-keyed, single-flight enrollment cache — 6 downloads per journey → 1, with invalidation on enroll/purchase/sign-out/account switch and no authorization ever cached.
* **Verified:** 122 test suites pass (0 failed), the new suite executes the cache and measures 6→1 / 3→1 rules, `npx tsc --noEmit` clean, ESLint 0 errors on changed files, security invariants asserted (lock behaviour, 20 s bound, exact allowlist, no access decision from cache).
* **Not verified:** `php -l` and PHP suites (no PHP binary here); and all absolute timings — cold launch, resume, per-screen render. A dev-build cold launch now prints `[Perf] cold launch timeline` with the five stage deltas, which is the fastest way to confirm on your iPhone which gate dominates before we spend effort on the payload/index work.
