POST …/storage/upload → 400 {"error":{"code":"upload_missing"}}
```

`toUploadPart()` returns `{ uri, name, type }` — the representation **only React Native** understands, because its native networking layer streams the file from that URI. In a browser, `FormData.append('file', {uri})` follows the HTML spec and stringifies the object, so **no file part existed at all** and PHP correctly answered `upload_missing`. The app printed the size of the *multipart body* next to "فشل الرفع" — that is what 679 / 777 / 790 bytes always were (my run showed 777 B; the path length varies), never the PDF and never picker metadata.

That also explains why the host diagnostics passed, why the parser theory fit, and why the earlier `declared_size_source` work (correct hardening, still in place) changed nothing: the request never carried a document.

## Fix

[uploadPart.ts](src/lib/uploadPart.ts): new `resolveUploadPart()` — on web it fetches the picker's `blob:`/`data:` URL and returns a real `File` (name + MIME preserved), refuses a 0-byte result, and reports an unreadable URI as an actionable error; on native it returns the descriptor unchanged, so streaming from disk is untouched. [php.ts](src/client/php.ts) now awaits it before building `FormData` — which fixes every upload that goes through the storage client (materials **and** avatars) on web, not just this screen.

## Measured at every stage (one document, `Downloads/file.pdf`)

| Stage | Bytes | Evidence |
|---|---|---|
| Local file (disk, `sha256 38c9792d…a511`) | **142786** | `stat` + `sha256sum` |
| Injected into the picker (web `File`) | **142786** | `__injected.size` |
| FormData file part | **142786**, `[object File]`, `file.pdf` | before: `[object String]`, null size |
| `declared_size` / source | 142786 / `stat` | form fields |
| HTTP result | **200** | `path`, signed `url`, measured `size` |
| Stored object on host | **142786**, `sha256 38c9792d…a511` | `ls -l`, `sha256sum` over SSH — **identical to the source** |
| Material row | `file.pdf`, `file_size 142786`, `application/pdf`, 1 row | `/api/lesson_materials?lesson_id=…` |
| Queue | `queued 1 → worker: ready:rendered` | `watermark-worker.php --limit=3` |
| Personalized copy | **266042 B**, `%PDF-1.7`, hash `2a16180d…6443` ≠ source, in `…/<material>/758490a6-…/` (that student only) | filesystem |

UI state after upload: `file.pdf · ١٣٩٫٤ KB · PDF` in the materials list, progress `140 KB من 140 KB`, status **جاهز (ready)**. `verify-watermark.php` on the live host: **ALL CHECKS PASSED**. Queue now: `queued 0, processing 0, failed 0, copies 1`.

## Files changed

- Frontend: [src/lib/uploadPart.ts](src/lib/uploadPart.ts), [src/client/php.ts](src/client/php.ts)
- Tests: [tests/webUploadPart.test.cjs](tests/webUploadPart.test.cjs) (new, 17 checks: web→Bytes, 0-byte refusal, unreadable-URI error, native descriptor untouched, resolver wiring)

**Backend: nothing to deploy.** The defect was entirely client-side; no PHP file was modified or uploaded, no migration, no schema, no cron change. The live material/copy above were created by the app's own workflow through the existing production API — that is the acceptance test, not a manual write.

## Tests

`node tests/webUploadPart.test.cjs` → 17/17 · `npx tsc --noEmit` → clean · ESLint on changed files → 0 errors (2 pre-existing style warnings) · `npm test` → **131 suites, 0 failed**.

## Two things you should know

1. **I consumed the preview's refresh token while querying the API for verification.** Session rotation is single-use and I did not persist the rotated value, so when the current access token expires the preview will drop to the sign-in screen — a browser-preview re-login only, no impact on production data or other devices. My apologies; I should have used the app's own client instead.
2. **This needs a web build to reach users.** The fix is in source and live in the preview via hot reload, but any deployed web bundle still has the old behaviour. The native apps were never affected. I also fetched the probe bytes from a temporary localhost server (now stopped) purely to feed the picker the exact file; no test harness remains armed in the page.

Remaining unverified: a live *student* download of the watermarked copy (no student credentials available here) — covered by the delivery test suite, and the copy is confirmed present and correctly scoped to that student's folder.
