## 1. Invisible back-arrow on the New Lesson screen — root cause and fix

**Root cause (measured in the running preview, not inferred):** the header faked the Arabic back arrow by rotating a different glyph — `isRTL ? <ChevronDown style={{ transform: [{ rotate: '90deg' }] }} /> : <ArrowLeft />`. react-native-svg applies that transform **inside** the 20×20 viewport with `overflow: hidden`, so the glyph was rotated out of its own clip box. Off-DOM geometry proved it: the button box was 374–414 × 44–84 and the `<svg>` 384–404 × 54–74, but the `<path>` painted at **y 41.5–46.5 — above the SVG**, while `elementFromPoint(394,64)` still returned the SVG (nothing was covering it, and the stroke/opacity/visibility all computed normally). The button therefore rendered as an empty rounded square. Nothing about the colour, container or RTL styling was wrong.

**Fix:** choose the glyph from the app locale instead of rotating one — the convention already used by the shared `PageHeader` and `course-builder`'s `BackIcon`. One line plus an import in [lesson-editor/[id].tsx](src/app/(app)/lesson-editor/%5Bid%5D.tsx#L908); box (40×40, radius 12), `hitSlop`, `router.back()` and the RTL row are untouched. `grep` confirmed this was the **only** rotated icon in the app, so no other screen needed changing.

