Every rung reached its configured concurrency, so 200 concurrent requests were genuinely achieved — but as **anonymous boot traffic**, not signed-in students (see limitations).

**Proven bottleneck — `max_user_connections = 50`.** The 5xx are MariaDB per-user connection-quota errors, from the production log (`request_id`/timestamp sanitized, no user data): `SQLSTATE[HY000] [1226] User 'vcoafnqsgg_api' has exceeded the 'max_user_connections' resource`. Exactly **30** such errors exist in the log — 15 in the 150-VU minute, 15 in the 200-VU minute — matching k6's per-stage 5xx counts (13/15), while the server allows `max_connections = 500` and `Connection_errors_max_connections = 0`. Up to 100 VUs: zero errors, flat p50 ≈ 256 ms, 106 req/s. At 150 VUs p99 jumped to 776 ms; at 200 VUs p90 more than doubled (692 ms vs 279 ms) and p95 hit 797 ms. Nothing else broke — no 508s, no timeouts, `Threads_running` 8 after the run.

**Measured DB/host state:** `max_used_connections` 139, `Threads_connected` 62, `Aborted_connects` 1,147 (2 h uptime), `Slow_queries` 43, `Innodb_row_lock_waits` 159 (avg 7.2 ms), `Created_tmp_disk_tables` 201,730, buffer pool 118 MB, node load 22.7/24 cores, data volume 11 profiles / 6 courses. **Unavailable and stated as such:** CloudLinux LVE per-account CPU/entry-process/memory (no `lveinfo`/`lveps` on the account; the cPanel page is UI-only — so per-account CPU limits were never confirmed *or* refuted), PHP-FPM worker depth, per-query latency/count, DB CPU/memory/I/O — the app instruments none of them.

**Verdict:** the host serves 200 concurrent anonymous requests at ~169 req/s with p95 < 0.8 s, and the first real wall is the **50-connection DB quota**, reached between 100 and 150 concurrent requests. This is **not** evidence that MedAcademy supports 200 concurrent students: the workload was 4 public endpoints, the dataset is tiny (6 courses), one generator on one IP, ~30 s holds, and no video traffic. Raise/verify `max_user_connections` (or pool connections) before sizing for ≥150 simultaneous requests; below ~100 concurrent requests the host showed no strain.

Remaining gap: the authenticated student journey could not be measured because production has **no dedicated test account** (read-only query: 0 `loadtest.*`/`test*` accounts; 7 real students). `issue-tokens.php` refuses to mint fixtures when `APP_ENV=production`, and driving 200 VUs from a real student's session would hammer production under their identity, so I added `SESSION_MODE=none` to the existing suite for exactly this case rather than reusing an account. The pool/login modes are ready the moment you provide a disposable account or a staging install.

**Files:** [plan.mjs](scripts/loadtest/lib/plan.mjs), [config.js](scripts/loadtest/lib/config.js), [student-journey.js](scripts/loadtest/student-journey.js), [README.md](scripts/loadtest/README.md) (new `SESSION_MODE=none` + corrected default/ceiling 200), [loadtestPlan.test.cjs](tests/loadtestPlan.test.cjs) (+P14), [LIVE_HOST_CAPACITY_TEST.md](docs/LIVE_HOST_CAPACITY_TEST.md) (full report), [lesson-editor/[id].tsx](src/app/(app)/lesson-editor/%5Bid%5D.tsx), [lessonEditorBackIcon.test.cjs](tests/lessonEditorBackIcon.test.cjs). Raw artifacts in `scripts/loadtest/results/live-*` (git-ignored).

**Checks:** `npx tsc --noEmit` clean; ESLint 0 errors on both changed files; **full suite 132 passed, 0 failed** (re-run after all edits); load-test plan suite 91/91. Reproduce a rung with `BASE_URL=https://api.medacademy.site LOADTEST_APPROVED=1 SESSION_MODE=none THINK_TIME_MS=1500 MAX_VUS=50 node scripts/loadtest/run-stages.cjs --approve-live --stages=50 --stage-ramp=15 --stage-hold=30`.

**Production untouched:** no file uploaded, no schema/record/PHP-setting/cron change, no sign-in (so no session created or revoked), no student data read (all four endpoints are public). The only side effects were the load itself and the 30 `Database connection failed` log lines it produced. One caveat on the preview: the doctor lesson-editor route is no longer reachable from the browser preview — it now carries a student session and redirects to `/dashboard` — so the icon was verified at 440 px and 390 px widths rather than at a 1440 px viewport; the button is a fixed 40×40 box, and the fix removed the only width-independent failure mode.

Next, I can raise the DB connection ceiling question with evidence or harden the tooling.
